.TH PM_GPSINFO 1 "March 2026" "v0.9.10" "PathMux Suite - GPS Inspector"
.SH NAME
pm_gpsinfo \- GPS metadata inspector for dashcam footage segments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pm_gpsinfo
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIfile.ts\fR
.br
.B pm_gpsinfo
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIMID\fR:\fITID\fR
.br
.B pm_gpsinfo
.B \-\-scan\-all\-trips
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pm_gpsinfo
reads GPS metadata from a dashcam footage segment using ExifTool and reports
the GPS lock time, first fix coordinates, and optionally all GPS records.
It can also batch-scan every trip across all cached manifests to report
seconds-to-GPS-lock for fleet analysis.
.PP
The tool operates in three modes:
.TP
.B Single-file mode
Probes one \fI.ts\fR segment and reports the GPS lock event and (optionally)
all GPS records from that file.
.TP
.B MID:TID mode
Resolves a manifest trip address to the first Front camera segment and
probes that file.  Equivalent to passing the absolute path directly.
.TP
.B Batch mode
.RB ( \-\-scan\-all\-trips )
Reads all cached manifests, scans the first Front segment of each trip,
and prints a table of GPS lock times.  Lock times are written back into
each manifest for display in the interactive browser and
.BR pm_ls (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Single-file and MID:TID options"
.TP
.B \-\-first\-lock
Report the first GPS record with a valid (non-zero) fix.  This is the
default mode.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Report all GPS records from the segment, not just the first lock.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format (default).
.TP
.B \-\-text
Output in human-readable text format.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output in comma-separated values format.
.TP
.B \-\-xml
Output in XML format.
.SS "Batch scan options"
.TP
.B \-\-scan\-all\-trips
Scan the first Front camera segment of every trip across all cached
manifests.  Prints a table showing manifest ID, trip ID, nominal segment
duration, seconds to first GPS lock, and the segment filename.  Results are
written back into each manifest (the
.B gpsLockSeconds
field) so subsequent tools do not need to re-scan.
.TP
.B \-\-scan\-all\-trips
cannot be combined with a file path or MID:TID argument.
.SS "Common options"
.TP
.BI \-\-exiftool " PATH"
Path to the ExifTool binary.  Defaults to
.B exiftool
(resolved via
.BR PATH ).
.TP
.BI \-\-exiftool\-opts " OPTIONS"
Override the ExifTool options string.  Defaults to the value stored in
.I ~/.config/pathmux/pathmux.json
.RB ( exiftoolOptions ).
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH "GPS LOCK"
GPS receivers require time to acquire a satellite fix after power-on
(cold start).  The first segment of a trip may contain records with
zero latitude and longitude while the receiver is searching.
.B pm_gpsinfo
scans forward through the GPS stream and reports the first record with a
non-zero fix.
.PP
A
.B first_lock_record
of
.B 0
means the receiver had a warm start and the fix was already valid at the
beginning of the segment (typical on short stop-and-go trips).  A value
greater than 0 is the record index of the first valid fix; dividing by the
GPS sample rate (one per second) gives seconds to lock.
.PP
A result of
.B none
means no valid fix was found in the segment at all.  This is normal for
very short stub segments recorded at startup before the GPS receiver acquired
a lock.
.SH "OUTPUT FORMATS"
.SS JSON (default)
.nf
{
  "file": "/path/to/Front/20260209_043838F.ts",
  "total_records": 147,
  "first_lock_record": 0,
  "first_lock": {
    "timestamp": "2026:02:09 10:39:14",
    "record_index": 0,
    "lat": 30.419000,
    "lon": -89.025191
  }
}
.fi
.SS Text
.nf
File:           /path/to/Front/20260209_043838F.ts
Total records:  147
Valid fixes:    147  (100% coverage)
First lock:     record 0  (0s after segment start)
  Timestamp:    2026:02:09 10:39:14
  Position:     30.419000, -89.025191
  Speed:        0.0 km/h
  Heading:      0.0\[de]
.fi
.PP
In
.B \-\-all
mode the text report also shows the last fix and a GPS dropout count.
.SH "SCAN-ALL-TRIPS OUTPUT"
.nf
MID  TID  SegDur  LockAt  First Segment
---  ---  ------  ------  --------------------
CY   7E     180s      0s  20260225_044424F.ts
CY   3Z     180s    none  20260225_035430F.ts
.fi
.PP
.B SegDur
is the nominal segment interval derived from filename timestamp spacing.
.B LockAt
is seconds to first GPS fix (0s = immediate; none = no fix found).
.SH NOTES
Timestamps in GPS output use the format
.B "YYYY:MM:DD HH:MM:SS"
in UTC, as returned by ExifTool.  Filename timestamps are in local time.
.PP
Speed is reported in km/h.  Altitude is present in the GPS stream but
known incorrect on the Pruveeo D90 (returns negative values at sea level)
and is therefore not reported.
.PP
GPS extraction requires ExifTool to be installed and the options string
to match the camera's GPS format.  If extraction returns no records,
verify your ExifTool installation.  If your camera's GPS format is not
supported by ExifTool, contact the ExifTool maintainer directly.
See
.BR exiftool (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pathmux/pathmux.json
Application settings including
.B exiftoolPath
and
.BR exiftoolOptions .
.TP
.I ~/.config/pathmux/manifests.json
Manifest index used by MID:TID resolution and
.BR \-\-scan\-all\-trips .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure (bad arguments, file not found, ExifTool error, or MID:TID not
resolved).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pathmux (1),
.BR pm_gpsexport (1),
.BR pm_ls (1),
.BR exiftool (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Developed by Steve Berg, 2026.
